<title>MEXICO: Mexico's one-month Cetes rate rises in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's one-month Cetes rate rises in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's one-month Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>29-Day	27.29	    + 27	    27.29     27.29</p>
<p>92-Day	26.57	    + 51	    26.28     26.74</p>
<p>183-Day     25.76	    -  5	    25.70     25.81</p>
<p>358-Day     25.59				25.48     25.84</p>
<p>Last week the 364-day paper was assigned at 25.46 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>29-Day	900 million pesos   3.16 bln pesos	 3.51</p>
<p>92-Day	900 million pesos   2.89 bln pesos	 3.21</p>
<p>183-Day     900 million pesos   4.02 bln pesos	 4.47</p>
<p>358-Day     600 million pesos   1.32 bln pesos	 2.20</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.45 compared with 3.88 the week before, on demand of 12.81 billion pesos last week.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    29-Day			 nil  basis points</p>
<p>    92-Day			  17  basis points</p>
<p>    183-Day			  5  basis points</p>
<p>    358-Day			 25  basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559.</p>
